-- The CoA change potions, restored.
--
-- Six change potions and three customization potions exist in the realm's own database (and in
-- the client's item cache: Ascension_LocalLoot lists all nine), but none of them has an
-- item_template row anywhere in this repository.  mod-ethereal-bazaar's generated convenience
-- list already sells three of them from Tiraxis --
--
--     (900008,24,910201,0,0,2984),  -- Customization Potion, 150 tokens
--     (900008,25,910200,0,0,2984),  -- Faction Change Potion, 150 tokens
--     (900008,26,200001,0,0,2984);  -- Race Change Potion, 150 tokens
--
-- -- and those three rows are dangling on a realm built from this tree: ObjectMgr::IsVendorItemValid
-- skips them ("have in item list non-existed item ..., ignore"), so the bazaar's vanity slots simply
-- come up empty.  The other six (200000, 505005, 505006, 97858, 2001181, 2001185) have no source at
-- all in tree: the webshop mailed the account-bound halves, which no realm can reconstruct.
--
-- Every field except ScriptName is the realm's own value: spellid_1 200164 for the eight potions
-- whose service the character-select screen applies (spell 200164 is the client's "Potion Visual",
-- effect 77 SPELL_EFFECT_SCRIPT_EFFECT, and is inert in the core), spellid_1 93216 for the class
-- potion, spellcharges_1 -1 (the core's single-use convention) except on the class potion (0), the
-- account-bound Flags 134217760 on the two "Soulbound" copies, FlagsExtra 2/1 (Alliance-only /
-- Horde-only) on the two seven-day faction potions.
--
-- ScriptName is the one field this restoration adds: it binds the module's item script, which is
-- what turns "Drink up!" into the service.  The rows are written as REPLACE INTO, so the statement
-- is idempotent: re-applying it restores the row to exactly this shape and touches nothing else.
--
-- Every value above was read back from the realm's own item_template row, field for field, and each
-- statement selects nothing and depends on no other row: the file restores the nine rows wherever
-- they are missing and leaves them exactly as they are wherever they already stand.

